{
  "name": "stag-beetle",
  "_about": "The stag beetle (Lucanus cervus), a male 5 cm long and 7 with its jaws: a broad flat black head carrying the huge chestnut-red ANTLER jaws -- curving in, a big tooth on the inside halfway along, the tip forked -- held up and open; elbowed antennae with a comb at the end; a broad black pronotum; glossy chestnut wing cases, parallel-sided; long black legs, the front tibiae toothed for digging. Variant: the female (small black jaws, a narrower head, 4 cm). Written whole by tools/creaturegen/rework/insects/beetles.py on insectlib.py (six jointed legs on a tripod gait, the antennae on bones of their own that wave).",
